# Agistra hub layout

This workspace is an **Agistra hub** — it holds planning, memory, and task queues for one or more projects. Project source code lives in sibling repositories.

## Directories

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `projects/<project>/` | Task files for a project — one Markdown file per task |
| `memory/<agent>.md` | Live HOT/WARM/COLD agent memory (tracked in repo — commit between sessions to persist state) |
| `memory/archive/` | Daily memory snapshots from end-of-day `dreaming` |
| `skills/<name>/` | Canonical skill corpus — full directory trees (scripts, assets, `SKILL.md`) |
| `.cursor/agents/` | Cursor agent profiles (generated — do not edit directly) |
| `.github/skills/<name>/` | VS Code/Copilot discovery stubs (`SKILL.md` only — points at `skills/<name>/`) |
| `.codex/skills/<name>/` | Codex discovery stubs (`SKILL.md` only — points at `skills/<name>/`) |
| `pipelines/deploy/` | Hub CLI — dispatch, scan, advance, launch, setup |
| `docs/` | Agent identity cards and skill reference |

## Task file naming

`task_N_<state>_<short-slug>.md` — N is sequential (1, 2, 3…), `<state>` is one of the lifecycle state tokens (todo, in-progress, ready-for-review, ready-for-qa, changes-requested, qa-passed, done), slug is lowercase kebab-case.

Example: `task_12_todo_security-hardening.md`

State is encoded in both the filename token and the `status:` frontmatter field (frontmatter is authoritative).

## CLI shortcuts

```bash
npm run dispatch -- <project>                         # Print current task prompt
npm run scan     -- <project>                         # Health scan + generate task files
npm run advance  -- <project>                         # Mark current task done, show next
npm run launch   -- <project>                         # Launch Claude in the project directory
node pipelines/deploy/index.js dispatch <project> --task 6  # Target a specific task by number
node pipelines/deploy/index.js scan <project> --dry-run     # Preview scan without writing files
```

## Invoking an agent

This hub folder must be open in your Cursor workspace for `@architect` to resolve:

```text
@architect Read .cursor/agents/architect.md. Then read memory/architect.md. Then: [your instruction]
```

If the short name doesn't resolve (hub folder not in workspace), use the explicit file path:

```text
@.cursor/agents/architect.md Read .cursor/agents/architect.md. Then read memory/architect.md. Then: [your instruction]
```

## Edit rules

- Edit agent profiles in the **source profiles repo**, then redeploy with `npm run deploy -- <hub-path>`.
- Edit task files directly in `projects/<project>/`.
- Never edit `.cursor/agents/`, `.github/skills/`, or `.codex/skills/` files by hand — they are generated stubs or adapter outputs.
- Dispatch and agents read full skill content from canonical `skills/` — not from stub paths.
- `memory/` files are tracked in the repo — commit between sessions to persist agent state.
